   "id": "P008",
   "texts": [
    "Amazon VPC",
    "An Amazon VPC is a virtual network",
    "provisioned in a logically isolated section",
    "of the AWS Cloud:",
    "Amazon VPC",
    "•",
    "Supports logical separation with subnets",
    "•",
    "Offers fine-grained security",
    "•",
    "Supports optional hardware virtual private",
    "network (VPN)"
   ],
   "notes": [],
   "hidden": false,
   "rendered": [],
   "img": "img/p-08.jpg"
  },
  {
   "id": "P009",
   "texts": [
    "Amazon VPC configuration: IP addressing",
    "IP addressing:",
    "• Valid private IP address ranges defined by RFC 1918",
    "• In an Amazon VPC, you can only define networks between /16",
    "and /28.",
    "Use non-overlapping IP address ranges.",
    "Best Practice",
    "Restrict VPCs to ranges defined in RFC1918 to avoid potential",
    "routing issues."
   ],
   "notes": [],
   "hidden": false,
   "rendered": [],
   "img": "img/p-09.jpg"
  },
